Flayr Tune patch for JUCE 8.0.16-security (ea77444750de45e036e0279bb0291144bf8e3688).

XmlDocument::readEntity, hex branch: on "&#x" followed by a non-hex character
it reports an error, carries on, and steps over that character. When the
character is the string's terminating null (input ending in "&#x", "&#x4",
...), parsing continues past the end of the buffer: a heap over-read that a
crafted project file could trigger in the host (found by tests/fuzz/fuzz_state
with ASan; minimal input "<e>&#x"). Stop at the end of the text instead
(the same code as Flayr Chop's fix, so both plug-ins ship the same JUCE).

Flayr Tune also refuses such blobs before parsing (isSafeStateBlob), so this
is defence in depth. Applied by CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND.

Flayr-Patch-Marker: modules/juce_core/xml/juce_XmlDocument.cpp FLAYR_PATCH juce-xml-entity-overread v2

